NAME
    install.sh - stage a GRUB UEFI image and external loader on an ESP

SYNOPSIS
    ./install.sh --stage DIR --esp DIR [--apply] [--allow-directory]

DESCRIPTION
    Installs one staged x86_64-efi or arm64-efi firmware executable
    and the shared source-controlled m-loader under a prepared FAT32 ESP.
    Does NOT partition, format, write boot sectors or require a data
    partition. By default only prints a plan; --apply writes files.

    Existing EFI firmware entries are never overwritten. An already
    present external loader is accepted only if its complete contents
    match the staged loader. Different installed loader trees are not
    merged or silently replaced. The ESP must be a mounted vfat volume.
    --allow-directory is only for disposable staging, not real media.

    i386-pc BIOS embedding is a separate build-image.sh responsibility,
    and is never performed through file copying by this command.

EXAMPLE
    ./install.sh --stage ./build/stages/x86_64-efi --esp /mnt/esp
    ./install.sh --stage ./build/stages/x86_64-efi --esp /mnt/esp --apply

SEE ALSO
    manual/build, manual/build-image, manual/usb-image
